 "narrative": "Compared to last report most reported forages sold steady except grass hay sold steady to 5.00 higher. Demand was moderate to good.  Some of the higher priced alfalfa hay continues to go to Wyoming ranchers. Corn stalks are going up in a rather slow pace for this time of year. But, crops have been slower to come out than previous years.  Some producers are hoping to have final cutting of alfalfa done by next week before a chance of moisture comes along.   Still acres of cane and millet hay to get dried down and baled.    A week early, Have a Happy Thanksgiving!",
